ent ministries, agencies, institutions or organizations, for purposes of promoting public health and safety and allowing emergency services personnel... to plan and respond properly in the event of an emergency.\"\n*   **6.7 Supplier Verification**:\n    *   **Addition**: Subsection 6.7 in V3 adds the sentence: \"OPA require verification of the identity of Supplier for the purposes of acknowledging agreement to amendments, assignments or any other matter relating to this Contract.\" (Note: grammatical error \"OPA require\" present in V3).\n\n**Section 7: Notices**\n*   **7.2 Change of Contact Information**: Wording change from \"by written notice to the other\" to \"by written notice **in the Prescribed Form** to the other.\"\n\n**Section 8: Termination**\n*   **8.1 On Notice**: Wording change from \"prior written notice to OPA\" to \"prior written notice **in the Prescribed Form** to OPA.\"\n\n**Section 9: Amendment**\n*   **Deletion/Wording Change**: V3 adds the requirement that the written agreement must be \"**in the Prescribed Form**.\"\n\n**Section 12: Dispute Resolution**\n*   **Addition**: V3 adds a substantial multi-paragraph section regarding \"Combined and Joined Disputes,\" allowing OPA to consolidate similar complaints or disputes from multiple suppliers for efficiency.\n*   **Minor Wording**: Added specific references to the \"Judicial District of Toronto Region,\" the \"City of Toronto,\" and explicit reference to the \"Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario).\"\n\n**Identical Sections**\n*   5.2 Metering (5.2.1, 5.2.2)\n*   5.3 Eligibility (5.3.1)\n*   6.1 Access Rights\n*   6.2 Electricity\n*   6.3 Meter and Meter Data (6.3.1, 6.3.2)\n*   6.4 Freedom of Information\n*   6.6 Statement Copies\n*   7.1 Address for Notice\n*   7.3 Timing of Notice\n*   8.2 For Breach\n*   8.3 Automatic\n*   10 Assignment\n*   11 Governing Law"} {:raw_diffs "### 1. General Provisions & Dispute Resolution (Part 2, Sections 12-14)\n*   **Arbitration Appointment (Section 12):** Identical text regarding the appointment of an Arbitrator and the role of the Ontario Superior Court of Justice.\n*   **Dispute Consolidation (Section 12):** Identical text regarding OPA's right to join/consolidate claims for efficiency.\n*   **LDC Failure to Pay (Section 13):** Identical text; OPA continues to guarantee Generation Payments subject to Supplier exhausting recourse against the LDC.\n*   **Suppliers Composed of Multiple Entities (Section 14):** \n    *   **Section 14.1:** Identical text regarding joint and several liability.\n    *   **Section 14.2:** Identical substantive requirements for removing natural persons. \n    *   **Wording Change (Section 14.2):** In the reference to joint and several liability, V2 refers to \"Section 14.1.1\" while V3 correctly refers to \"Section 14.1\".\n\n### 2. Appendix A - Definitions\n*   **Existing Definitions (Identical):** \"Abut\", \"Application\", \"Base Date\", \"Biogas\", \"Business Day\", \"Connection Agreement\", \"Connection Impact Assessment\", \"Connection Point\", \"Contract\", \"Contract Commencement Date\", \"Contract End Date\", \"Contract Price\", \"CPI\", \"Deemed Single Property\", \"Directly Connected Facility\", \"Distribution System Code\", \"Eligible Participant\", \"Eligible Participant Schedule\", \"Environmental Attributes\", \"Existing Generation Facility\", \"Facility\", \"FIT Price Schedule\", \"FIT Program\", \"FIT Program Facility\", \"Generation Payment\", \"Governmental Authority\", \"Indexed Contract Price\", \"Indirectly Connected Facility\", \"In Parallel\", \"ITA\", \"kWh\", \"Laws and Regulations\".\n*   **Deletion:** The definition for **\"Domestic Content Level\"** (which referenced Appendix C, Section 1.5 in V2) is entirely removed from Appendix A in Contract V3.\n*   **Formatting/Clarity (Deemed Single Property):** V3 removes the word \"Single\" from the quote marks in the term \"Deemed Single Property\" (formatting it as “Deemed Single Property” vs V2's “Deemed Single Property”).\n\n### 3. Appendix A - New Content in V3 (Not in Chunk)\n*   The following definitions appear in V3 Appendix A but were not present in the provided V2 chunk: **\"LDC\"**, **\"microFIT Rules\"**, **\"microFIT Program\"**, **\"Nameplate Capacity\"**, **\"Party/Parties\"**, **\"Percentage Escalated\"**, **\"Prescribed Form\"**, and **\"Project Eligibility Requirements\"**. (Note: The V2 chunk cuts off at \"Distributi...\")."} {:raw_diffs "The following specific changes were identified between the provided segment of Contract V2 (comprising the end of Appendix A, Appendix B, and the beginning of Appendix C) and the full Contract V3:\n\n### 1. Appendix A (Definitions)\n*   **Deemed Single Property**:\n    *   **V2**: Used standard list numbering (a), (b), (c), (d).\n    *   **V3**: Appends specific legal references to clause (b)(ii): \"Sections 50(3)(a), 50(3)(b), 50(3)(f), or 50(5)(a) of the **Planning Act (Ontario)**.\"\n*   **Existing Generation Facility**:\n    *   **V3 Addition**: New definition added: \"means an electricity generating facility that is located on the same property as the Facility and which is connected to the LDC distribution system.\"\n*   **Prescribed Form**:\n    *   **V3 Addition**: New definition added: \"means, in relation to a form, the latest version of the corresponding form appearing on the Website, as may be amended or replaced by the OPA from time to time and without notice to the Supplier.\"\n*   **Project Eligibility Requirements**:\n    *   **Clause (c)**: V3 adds \"unless otherwise consented to by the OPA in writing in its sole and absolute discretion.\"\n*   **Property Identification Number**:\n    *   **V2**: Referenced \"Land Titles Act R.S.O. 1990, c. L. 5, s. 141(2)\".\n    *   **V3**: Corrects/updates punctuation to \"Land Titles Act R.S.O. 1990, c. L. 5, s. 141(2).\" (identical text, verified).\n*   **Website**:\n    *   **V3 Addition**: New definition added identifying the microFIT URL.\n*   **Removed Definitions**: The definition for \"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" present in V2's Appendix A is **deleted** in V3's Appendix A.\n\n### 2. Appendix B (Calculation of Indexed Contract Price)\n*   **Mathematical Formula**:\n    *   **V2**: $\\text{CP}_y = \\text{CP} \\times [ (1 - \\text{PE}) + ( \\text{PE} \\times \\frac{\\text{CPI}_y}{\\text{CPI}_{\\text{BD}}} ) ]$\n    *   **V3**: Formula remains functionally identical but the visual rendering/typography in the V3 document uses a updated font style for the fraction $\\frac{\\text{CPI}_y}{\\text{CPI}_{\\text{BD}}}$.\n*   **Substantive Text**: The text in notes (a) and (b) and the variable definitions are **identical**.\n\n### 3. Appendix C (Solar Photovoltaic Schedule)\n*   **Definition of \"Existing Building\"**:\n    *   **V2**: Limited to buildings completely constructed on the date the Application was first submitted.\n    *   **V3**: Expanded to include a second clause: \"(b) in respect of which the OPA has, in its sole and absolute discretion, issued a written confirmation that the building will be deemed an Existing Building...\"\n*   **Domestic Content Requirements**:\n    *   **V2**: Included detailed sections 1.1 through 1.7 and two exhaustive \"Domestic Content Grids\" (Crystalline Silicon and Thin-Film) listing specific qualifying percentages for components like Silicon, Inverters, and Framing.\n    *   **V3**: **Entirely deleted** the Domestic Content Requirement sections (1.1-1.7) and the associated Tables 1 and 2 from Appendix C. Appendix C in V3 now only contains the definitions for \"Existing Building\" and \"Rooftop Facility.\"\n\n### 4. Structuring/Formatting\n*   **Page References**: V2's segment spans pages 14 through 18. The corresponding definitions and Appendix B/C in V3 are located on pages 12 through 18, reflecting the overall expansion of the contract (V3 includes more comprehensive schedules like Appendix D-1, D-2, and E)."} {:raw_diffs "### 1. Deletions (Present in Chunk, Absent in V3)\n*   **Domestic Content Grids:** The domestic content requirements for Solar Photovoltaic Power Projects (referenced as Table 3 and associated qualifying percentages in the chunk) have been entirely removed. Contract V3 does not contain these tables or the specific \"Designated Activity\" manufacturing requirements for Ontario content.\n*   **Appendix E, Section 1 - \"Transmission System Code\" Definition:** The definition of \"Transmission System Code\" found in Appendix E of the chunk is deleted in the Appendix E of V3.\n\n### 2. Additions (Present in V3, Absent in Chunk)\n*   **Appendix C - Solar Photovoltaic Schedule:** The chunk contained manufacturing grids; however, V3 Appendix C is replaced with a new \"Solar Photovoltaic Schedule\" (V3 Page 18) that defines \"Existing Building\" and \"Rooftop Facility.\"\n\n### 3. Wording and Structural Changes\n*   **Appendix D-1 (Directly Connected Facility Schedule):**\n    *   **Section 1 heading:** Corrected from \"REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTES\" (chunk) to \"REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES\" (V3 Page 19).\n*   **Appendix E (LDC Supplier Schedule):**\n    *   **Section 1 (\"IESO\" Definition):** The chunk includes \"of Ontario established under Part II of the Electricity Act or its successor.\" V3 (Page 21) abbreviates this to \"established under Part II of the Electricity Act or its successor.\"\n    *   **Section 3.1(a):** Wording change from \"orders -in-council\" (chunk) to \"orders- in-council\" (V3 Page 21) regarding hyphenation.\n    *   **Section 3.1(b):** The word \"Person\" (capitalized in chunk) is changed to \"person\" (lowercase in V3 Page 21).\n\n### 4. Identical Sections\n*   **Appendix D-1, Sections 1.1, 2.1, and 2.2** regarding battery back-up and directly connected status are identical.\n*   **Appendix D-2, Sections 1 and 2** (Indirectly Connected Facility Schedule) including the \"In Parallel\" definition and the diagrams for battery back-up configurations are identical.\n*   **Appendix E, Sections 2.1, 2.2, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4, 3.5, and 3.6** are identical in substance and wording."}]}, :node-id #uuid "6bdb7abe-f22f-411e-8eb4-336252a4701b", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-started, :sheet-id #uuid "5241eb9d-a207-4d82-a629-77059bb1f90e", :event/id #uuid "019e431c-4f59-7046-97f6-f3b90dd72cc0"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YWfb7qSqPCYbIBblj8WE4FyxK8_fy", :mulog/timestamp 1779242389338, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YWfb7qSqPCYbIBblj8WE4FyxK8_fy", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
